/**
 * Dev-only stand-ins for a finished /api/preview job.
 *
 * The pipeline needs a live store and a headless Chrome, neither of which is
 * available while this page is being built or screenshotted — so PreviewStage
 * accepts `?fixture=<key>` outside production and renders these instead.
 *
 * Three of them, because the before/after comparison has more shapes than the
 * widget does and each one has to be looked at:
 *
 *   light    real screenshot, real catalogue, and the store's own search box
 *            opened and photographed empty. The common case, and the one the
 *            comparison exists for.
 *   bare     `nativeSearch: null` — no search control we could open, so there
 *            is no before state and no toggle; the stage is the Growsearch
 *            mock-up alone.
 *   dark     the degraded end: no browser, no products, synthesised storefront.
 *            No browser also means no search capture, so this is null too —
 *            the search screenshot comes from the same Chrome as the homepage
 *            one and cannot exist without it.
 *
 * There is deliberately no fixture of their search *answering* anything. The
 * job no longer types a query — see `NativeSearch` in types.ts for why — and
 * a fixture of a results page would let this panel be built and reviewed
 * against exactly the image it must never show.
 *
 * The homepage screenshot is a 720x450 JPEG rendered from a mock storefront
 * and scaled up by the frame. The frame dims it in the after state anyway, so
 * the smaller file is indistinguishable and keeps this module a sane size.
 * The search screenshot is a full 1440x900 capture of the same mock with its
 * search drawer open — the before state shows it undimmed, edge to edge, so a
 * half-size image would be visibly soft in exactly the state the panel exists
 * for.
 */

